# C33 remediation after attempt-01 (9/7/8/7/7, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 a case-bound scan could record a result on a specification | A scan may name only a Runtime Security case of the tenant's open library: a missing, another tenant's or another product's case is refused (`InvalidInput`) before anything is sent; at settlement the case must still be a Runtime case holding exactly what was scanned. A result stored on any non-Runtime case (and an oversized pack name) is dropped when a library is read, never shown. Tests: `starter_packs_are_named_…` now names a specification with its own exact prompt and response and an unknown case, both refused with no request sent and no result, across a restart; unit `a_stored_result_on_a_specification_or_an_oversized_pack_is_dropped_on_load` | `authority.rs`, `library.rs`, `ui_v2_workbench` |
| R2 call metadata unbounded against the parser | One bounded recording function (`recorded_request`, `header_names`): header names longer than 64 characters left out, at most 128 names, path cut at 2048 characters, method at most 16, HTTPS origins only (nothing else recorded), content type at most 128; the validator accepts exactly these (HTTP token methods, status 100-999). Tests: unit `a_recorded_call_stays_within_the_contracts_bounds` (long and many names, long path with a query, non-HTTPS); the integration test's service now answers with a 65-character and a 64-character header name (only the latter recorded); the component test "accepts every call within the core's bounds and refuses one past them" parses the bounds through `parseShellSnapshot` | `transport.rs`, `client.ts`, tests |
| R3 the library's workflows missing from v2 | Test Cases keeps C12's workflows: New case (Runtime with profile and application, specifications with a payload), Add starter packs, Add public examples, Import…, Export…, Remove per case (a full library can free a slot) and explicit Copy to another tenant (chosen in "Copy cases to"). Specifications still dispatch no scan. Test: "creates Runtime and specification cases, removes one at the limit, imports, exports and copies to another tenant, never scanning" | `test-cases.tsx`, `copy.ts` |
| R4 storage and outcome states ignored | The library's unsaved state (with Save again), load failure (with Open the library again and the failure's reason), problem (full, all present, …) and notice are shown, and dispatch outcomes are reported. Tests: component "says when the library is not saved, cannot open, is full or already holds the examples, and offers the recovery"; core `unsaved_packs_and_results_stay_shown_and_a_retry_keeps_them_across_a_restart` (a blocked write of a starter pack and of a case result: unsaved, both shown, Save again, then both survive a restart) | `test-cases.tsx`, `ui_v2_workbench` |
| R5 API Client not re-skinned | A layout context (`V2Layout`, provided by the v2 wrapper) makes the workbench's shared components take the v2 layout without editing the owner-held view: the page heading becomes the v2 title row, and the request editor puts method, URL, Send and Save on one line with the request details beside a response pane (stacked when narrow); the legacy layout is unchanged (its 22 workbench tests pass). Test: the V2-T14 test asserts the title row, the request line, the response pane holding the body and the status region outside it | `shell/presentation.ts`, `feature-view.tsx`, `document-editor.tsx`, `api-client.tsx`, provenance P52 |
| E2 native keyboard for both screens | C33-N04 now also drives the API Client by keyboard (Tab from the URL to Send, Space sends, the completion announced, the ring on Send, 900×600 at 200% in both themes) and the calls panel (ring on its control, Space hides it) | `acceptance_c33.py`, native-checks.json |
| Optional: calls note | The note says it shows the newest 50 calls | `copy.ts` |

The first attempt-01 check runs failed on (a) the evidence scripts copied without their executable bit (fixed) and (b) six `harness_identity_history` tests whose engines did not start within the desk's 1 s bootstrap limit when 30 tests start engines at once on this Mac (each passes alone; two test threads, or a 5 s limit, pass all 30). The shared test desk now allows 5 s; the bootstrap-timeout case still times out as expected.

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).
